[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1858","stub":{"id":"1858","section":"01. Moon Lake to Bridge to Yellowstone River","altname":"","river":"Lake Fork","difficulty":"IIItoIV","states":["USA-UTA"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"low-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"230","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112049","location":{"latitude":"40.559979","longitude":"-110.487509"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117326","location":{"latitude":"40.466","longitude":"-110.379997"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"8.3","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"tBFaSla1mYeIa6UeXcMFr","ext":"jpg","post_id":"MdOVVCA5obK2I0oxUZo5b","description":"You can scrape over the rocks on the right side of this rapid. The left side has a hole. It is an easy scout from the right bank. ","caption":"Second drop","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Cody Redmond","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-02-19T15:55:21.000Z","updated_at":"2024-02-19T15:55:21.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/tBFaSla1mYeIa6UeXcMFr","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/tBFaSla1mYeIa6UeXcMFr"}},{"id":"UUJKKZJSN4yQ8Pn3XEl4k","ext":"jpg","post_id":"MdOVVCA5obK2I0oxUZo5b","description":"Big pool area below the dam. ","caption":"The put in ","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Cody Redmond","poi_id":"112049","photo_date":"2024-02-19T15:55:21.000Z","updated_at":"2024-02-19T15:55:21.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/UUJKKZJSN4yQ8Pn3XEl4k","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/UUJKKZJSN4yQ8Pn3XEl4k"}},{"id":"lv3ZiFl8kvjolesC8IfGB","ext":"jpg","post_id":"MdOVVCA5obK2I0oxUZo5b","description":"The line is pretty much donw the middle on this drop, Get a late boof stroke in. Keeping the bow high. ","caption":"First Drop","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Cody Redmond","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-02-19T15:55:21.000Z","updated_at":"2024-02-19T15:55:21.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/lv3ZiFl8kvjolesC8IfGB","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/lv3ZiFl8kvjolesC8IfGB"}}],"detail":{"id":"1858","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"This run can receive dam release flows in the 300 cfs range in the summer, which makes for continuous and scenic whitewater, as an intrepid local packraft explorer, Scott England reported on July 18, 2015.\n\nThere is a dirt road right below the dam that could be a possible putin, although access is unclear, please be respectful.\n\nDevin Peterson paddled this run with a group in 2018, around 350 cfs (and 275 cfs, also a good level) and reported:\n\nThe best drops are just below the lake. You can scout them using a dirt turnoff. [https://goo.gl/maps/TBkSNTqsec82](https://goo.gl/maps/TBkSNTqsec82)\n\n10/2/2018, the log situation is improved, still worth a scout as always.\n\nHere is a video of the run: [https://youtu.be/QkXNu7bxu1c](https://youtu.be/QkXNu7bxu1c)\n\nSummer 2018 report:\n\nThere was a scary riverwide log just below the put in. First time the river braids you can take the right channel with less water, to avoid it. There was another mandatory portage a few miles down with easy takeout on the right. Once you get to the diversion you can hop on the canal going off the right to get back to the road. If you don't you'll end up in endless log jams and braiding. [https://goo.gl/maps/bQAvXncpLDp](https://goo.gl/maps/bQAvXncpLDp)\n\nThe run is just over 2 hours drive from Salt Lake.\n\nThis section seems to be about 2.3 miles.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"10.8","correlations":[{"reachID":"1858","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommend